## File Operations

### Read

Reads file contents from the local filesystem.

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `path` | string | Yes | Absolute path to the file |
| `offset` | integer | No | Line number to start reading from (1-indexed) |
| `limit` | integer | No | Number of lines to read |

**When to use**: Reading any file, including images (jpeg/jpg, png, gif, webp) and PDFs.

### Write

Creates or overwrites a file.

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `path` | string | Yes | Absolute path to the file |
| `contents` | string | Yes | File contents to write |

**When to use**: Creating new files or completely overwriting existing files. **Never use for incremental edits** -- use StrReplace instead.

### StrReplace

Performs exact string replacements in files.

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `path` | string | Yes | Absolute path to the file |
| `old_string` | string | Yes | Text to replace (must be unique in file) |
| `new_string` | string | Yes | Replacement text |
| `replace_all` | boolean | No | Replace all occurrences (default: false) |

**When to use**: Modifying existing file contents. **Always read the file first** before editing.

### Delete

Deletes a file at the specified path.

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `path` | string | Yes | Absolute path to the file |

**When to use**: Removing files that are no longer needed.

### EditNotebook

Edits Jupyter notebook cells.

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `target_notebook` | string | Yes | Path to the notebook file |
| `cell_idx` | integer | Yes | Cell index (0-based) |
| `is_new_cell` | boolean | Yes | true to create new cell, false to edit existing |
| `cell_language` | string | Yes | Cell language (python, markdown, javascript, typescript, r, sql, shell, raw, other) |
| `old_string` | string | Yes | Text to replace (required when is_new_cell=false) |
| `new_string` | string | Yes | Replacement text or new cell content |

**When to use**: Creating, editing, or deleting Jupyter notebook cells.

