## Search & Discovery

### Glob

Searches for files matching a glob pattern.

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `glob_pattern` | string | Yes | Glob pattern (e.g., `**/*.ts`, `src/components/**/*`) |
| `target_directory` | string | No | Absolute path to search directory (defaults to workspace root) |

**When to use**: Finding files by name pattern. **Use Grep for content search**, Glob for file name search.

### Grep

Powerful search tool built on ripgrep for searching file contents.

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `pattern` | string | Yes | Regex pattern to search for |
| `path` | string | No | File or directory to search in |
| `glob` | string | No | Glob pattern filter (e.g., `*.js`, `*.{ts,tsx}`) |
| `output_mode` | string | No | "content", "files_with_matches", or "count" (default: "content") |
| `-B` | number | No | Lines before each match |
| `-A` | number | No | Lines after each match |
| `-C` | number | No | Lines before and after each match |
| `-i` | boolean | No | Case insensitive search |
| `type` | string | No | File type (js, py, rust, go, java, etc.) |
| `head_limit` | number | No | Limit output size |
| `offset` | number | No | Skip first N entries |
| `multiline` | boolean | No | Enable multiline matching |

**When to use**: Searching file contents by text or regex. **Always use Grep over shell `grep` or `rg` commands** -- it's faster and more reliable.

### SemanticSearch

Semantic search that finds code by meaning, not exact text.

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `query` | string | Yes | Natural language question (e.g., "How does authentication work?") |
| `target_directories` | string[] | No | Limit search to specific directories |

**When to use**: Exploring unfamiliar codebases, asking "how does X work?" questions, finding code by concept rather than keyword. **Use Grep for exact text matches**, SemanticSearch for conceptual queries.

