## Execution

### Shell

Executes commands in a shell session.

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `command` | string | Yes | Command to execute |
| `working_directory` | string | No | Absolute path to working directory |
| `block_until_ms` | number | No | How long to wait before backgrounding (default: 30000ms) |
| `description` | string | No | Short description of the command |
| `notify_on_output` | object | No | Output monitoring config (pattern, reason, debounce_ms) |

**When to use**: Running system commands (git, npm, pip, docker, etc.). **Always use the Shell tool over running `grep`, `find`, `cat`, `head`, or `tail` commands** -- prefer the specialized tools for those operations.

### AwaitShell

Checks or polls a backgrounded shell job.

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `shell_id` | string | No | Shell ID to poll (required when block_until_ms=0) |
| `block_until_ms` | number | No | Max sleep time (default: 30000ms) |
| `pattern` | string | No | Block until regex matches stdout/stderr |

**When to use**: Polling backgrounded commands. **Only poll when actively blocked on a result** -- use completion notifications otherwise.

