## Agent Orchestration

### Task

Launches specialized subagents for complex tasks.

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `description` | string | Yes | User-friendly title for the subagent |
| `prompt` | string | Yes | Detailed task description with all context |
| `model` | string | No | Model slug (e.g., composer-2.5-fast) |
| `resume` | string | No | Agent ID to resume, or "self" to fork |
| `readonly` | boolean | No | Default false; if true, agent cannot modify files |
| `subagent_type` | enum | Yes | generalPurpose, explore, shell, cursor-guide, ci-investigator, bugbot, security-review, best-of-n-runner |
| `file_attachments` | string[] | No | Optional array of image/video paths |
| `interrupt` | boolean | No | Default false; interrupt running agent |
| `run_in_background` | boolean | No | Default false; run independently |

**When to use**: Multi-step tasks, codebase exploration, parallel approaches, specialized reviews. See [Agent Hierarchy](02-agent-hierarchy.mdc) for full details.

### TodoWrite

Creates and manages a structured task list.

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `todos` | object[] | Yes | Array of todo items with id, content, status |
| `merge` | boolean | Yes | true to merge with existing, false to replace |

**When to use**: Complex multi-step tasks (3+ distinct steps). **Do not use** for simple single-step tasks.

