## Parameter Patterns

### Working Directories

Most tools support an optional `working_directory` parameter for running in a specific directory:

```
Shell(command="npm install", working_directory="/path/to/project")
```

### Timeouts

The `block_until_ms` parameter controls how long to wait before backgrounding:

| Value | Behavior | Use Case |
|---|---|---|
| 30000 (default) | Wait up to 30 seconds | Short commands |
| 0 | Immediately background | Long-running processes (dev servers, watchers) |
| Custom | Wait specific duration | Commands with known runtime |

### Notifications

The `notify_on_output` parameter monitors terminal output:

```json
{
  "pattern": "Server running on port",
  "reason": "Dev server startup",
  "debounce_ms": 5000
}
```

### Smart Mode Approval

When auto-review blocks a tool call:

```json
{
  "requestSmartModeApproval": true,
  "smartModeBlockReason": "Exact block reason from auto-review"
}
```

